// commerce.payout.v1 — what the platform owes each marketplace shop.
//
// A payout is created when an order confirms (consumed from
// commerce.order.confirmed): the order's lines are grouped by shop_id (see
// commerce.fulfillment.v1's identical grouping for shipments) and one Payout
// is created per distinct marketplace shop, for the sum of that shop's line
// totals. First-party lines (shop_id "") create no payout — the platform
// already holds that revenue directly.
//
// v1 ships a SANDBOX settlement: a background sweep marks a PENDING payout
// PAID after a short delay, mirroring fulfillment's sandbox carrier. In
// production the sweep is replaced by a real payout-provider integration
// (e.g. Stripe Connect transfers) — the emitted events are identical either
// way. v1 also takes no platform commission: a payout is 100% of the shop's
// line total for that order; a fee/commission model is a deliberate later
// refinement (see ADR-043).

